Phase 1 specification is complete. The repository contained only a minimal README, so I wrote the two foundation documents from scratch and committed them to `main`.

**SPEC.md** defines Snippet Vault as a local-first, single-user snippet manager: seven prioritized user flows, explicit v1 non-goals (no auth, cloud sync, syntax highlighting, gist import, etc.), and a lean stack chosen for speed and testability — **TypeScript + Fastify + better-sqlite3 (FTS5) + esbuild-bundled vanilla client + Vitest**. Architecture covers directory layout, module boundaries, API contract, and a fixed quality bar (`lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build`, `dev`).

**ROADMAP.md** defines six milestones: M1 walking skeleton through M6 polish/release readiness. Each has checkable acceptance criteria tied to commands or URLs. M1 is scaffold-only; snippet features start at M2.

```json
{
  "stack": "Node.js 20+ / TypeScript / Fastify / better-sqlite3 (FTS5) / vanilla TS client (esbuild) / Vitest",
  "milestones": [
    { "id": "M1", "title": "Walking skeleton" },
    { "id": "M2", "title": "SQLite schema and snippet CRUD API" },
    { "id": "M3", "title": "Full-text search API" },
    { "id": "M4", "title": "Snippet list and create/edit UI" },
    { "id": "M5", "title": "Live search and copy-to-clipboard" },
    { "id": "M6", "title": "Polish and release readiness" }
  ],
  "open_questions_decided": [
    "Frontend: vanilla TypeScript bundled with esbuild (no React/Vue) to keep dependencies minimal per operator constraint",
    "Search engine: SQLite FTS5 with triggers (not LIKE queries) for instant as-you-type results",
    "Snippet IDs: UUID v4 generated server-side",
    "Tags storage: JSON array in SQLite column; comma-separated input in UI; flattened into FTS index",
    "Database path: ./data/snippets.db (gitignored, created on first run)",
    "Default port: 3000 (configurable via PORT env var)",
    "Delete UX: browser confirm dialog before permanent removal",
    "API validation: Fastify JSON Schema at route layer; 400/404/500 error shapes defined in SPEC"
  ]
}
```
